# CRM — project overview

An open-source, agentic-first CRM. The durable research agent is the product;
the database is where it writes things down. Single-tenant and internal by
design (Google sign-in + one allow-list).

## Monorepo layout (Turborepo on Bun)

| Path            | What it is                                              |
| --------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |
| `apps/agent`    | The research agent — tools, skills, schedules, sandbox |
| `apps/app`      | Next.js front end · http://localhost:3000              |
| `apps/api`      | NestJS API — HTTP, auth, tRPC, Google sync · :3001     |
| `packages/db`   | Prisma schema, migrations, shared Postgres client      |
| `packages/auth` | Better Auth config and the sign-in allow-list          |
| `packages/ui`   | shadcn/ui components, the Tailwind theme               |
| `packages/env`  | Finds and loads the root `.env`                        |

## Three rules the codebase holds to

- **Intelligence never lives in the API** (`docs/api.md`). Nest reports that
  something happened by writing a queue row; the agent decides what it means.
  A Nest service that calls an enrichment API is treated as a bug.
- **`packages/ui` is the only source of UI** (`docs/design.md`). No overriding
  styles at the call site.
- **There are no organizations.** Single tenant, deliberately. Do not add an
  `organizationId`.

## The agent's own rule

Nothing about a person is guessed. No tool accepts a confidence score. Tools
report what they observed; a ledger prices the evidence. Strong evidence writes
to the record, weak evidence becomes a suggestion a human settles.

## Active track: Sage CRM interface layer (Phase 7)

This fork is growing into an improvement layer OVER Sage CRM (on-prem, reached
via the `eware.dll` SOAP web service). The team runs sales in Sage — companies,
people, opportunities, and **forecasting** — and this app aims to be a nicer
surface on top, syncing bidirectionally (pull first, push later).

- Read `docs/plans/sage-crm-sync.md` before any Sage work. SOAP access + field
  mappings are confirmed against production; scope/decisions live there.
- Sage sync is MECHANICAL, so it lives in `apps/api/src/sage/` (mirrors the
  Google/Microsoft modules) — the "intelligence never in the API" rule still
  holds.
- **Forecasting is opportunity-driven in Sage** (deal value + certainty% + target
  close), not a separate record. The team enters the deal value in Sage
  `forecast` (their `total` is unused/empty), so local `Deal.amount` ← `forecast`
  and `weightedAmount` = `amount` × `certainty` (corrected 2026-08-02 — the
  original total/forecast assumption was backwards). `Deal` also carries
  `probability` / `dealType` / `sageStage` / `sageStatus`; the overview shows a
  forecast by close month (weighted vs unweighted).
- **7.4b full pull is DONE** (2026-08-02): ~14.2k companies / ~24.8k contacts /
  525 deals imported by the local one-shot `apps/api/scripts/sage-backfill.ts`;
  `phase = incremental`, nightly cron wired. Company/contact owners come from
  Sage `acctmgr` (name match). **Push write-back is BUILT** (outbox + echo-guard);
  remaining Sage work (reconcile soft-deactivate, nested field push) is
  DESIGN-ONLY / deferred. See `docs/plans/sage-crm-sync.md` and
  `HANDOFF-SAGE-SYNC.md`.
- **Pipeline pulse (DONE 2026-08-03)**: overview change feed + stuck deals +
  pipeline AI chat. Sage pull (non-echo) appends `DealFieldChange` rows with
  `source: sage`. Plan: `docs/plans/pipeline-pulse.md`.

